# PostgreSQL SQL Guidelines

Naming and schema:
- use snake_case identifiers
- keep names descriptive and unambiguous
- use schema qualification when it improves clarity

DDL conventions:
- define primary keys and constraints explicitly
- include indexes for frequent filtered/joined paths
- add comments for non-obvious table/purpose choices when helpful

Query quality:
- prioritize readable formatting and explicit aliases
- use CTEs when they improve comprehension of complex logic
- document non-obvious business SQL behavior

Safety:
- enforce tenant predicates in multi-tenant paths
- avoid hidden logic relying on implicit DB defaults
